                                                "example_id": "1a2008dc-3e4b-45b3-8cea-6c40a567c2cf",
                                                "sense_id": "e5136f76-55ff-3065-b10f-34aaa1cbf85d",
                                                "text": "You should start dating so you can find a suitable husband."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40cfbbef-e820-45b2-9ccc-94c2af18723f",
                                                "sense_id": "e5136f76-55ff-3065-b10f-34aaa1cbf85d",
                                                "text": "The husband and wife are one person in law."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4de7dafe-2605-45a5-a8c4-93b1f009cfc1",
                                                "sense_id": "e5136f76-55ff-3065-b10f-34aaa1cbf85d",
                                                "text": "A great bargain also had been[…]the arm-chair in which Bunting now sat forward, staring into the dull, small fire. In fact, that arm-chair had been an extravagance of Mrs. Bunting. She had wanted her husband to be comfortable after the day's work was done, and she had paid thirty-seven shillings for the chair."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5a7ae7e-af71-4a03-b5e8-b5bcbd09d090",
                                                "sense_id": "e5136f76-55ff-3065-b10f-34aaa1cbf85d",
                                                "text": "But Sophia's mother was not the woman to brook defiance. After a few moments' vain remonstrance her husband complied. His manner and appearance were suggestive of a satiated sea-lion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "add2cb35-e30d-3377-8468-47c1ba035bdc",
                                        "entry_id": "8d0fb453-501e-3368-8251-ef83d1218bb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A manager of property; one who has the care of another's belongings, owndom, or interests; a steward; an economist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1c4438f-d2b7-36ef-9bc2-672df6fc21a9",
                                        "entry_id": "8d0fb453-501e-3368-8251-ef83d1218bb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A prudent or frugal manager."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ad9ce3e-3f05-4ec4-a436-a541f3e1e745",
                                                "sense_id": "e1c4438f-d2b7-36ef-9bc2-672df6fc21a9",
                                                "text": "God knows how little time is left me, and may I be a good husband, to improve the short remnant thereof."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66f3d6dd-4385-4455-b306-1e96a288d93a",
                                                "sense_id": "e1c4438f-d2b7-36ef-9bc2-672df6fc21a9",
                                                "text": "[S]o I went and fetch’d a good Dram of Rum, and gave him; for I had been ſo good a Husband of my Rum, that I had a great deal left: When he had drank it, I made him take the two Fowling-Pieces, which we always carry’d, and load them with large Swan-Shot, as big as ſmall Piſtol Bullets; then I took four Muſkets, and loaded them with two Slugs, and five ſmall Bullets each; and my two Piſtols I loaded with a Brace of Bullets each; I hung my great Sword as uſual, naked by my Side, and gave Friday his Hatchet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c77de7b7-5727-3add-b90d-e0b7402a7621",
                                        "entry_id": "8d0fb453-501e-3368-8251-ef83d1218bb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The master of a house; the head of a family; a householder."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78fbca52-16fd-3760-b48e-bca1966a9bbd",
                                        "entry_id": "8d0fb453-501e-3368-8251-ef83d1218bb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tiller of the ground; a husbandman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4afda87a-2f79-469c-aa1e-63507e2b1ba7",
                                                "sense_id": "78fbca52-16fd-3760-b48e-bca1966a9bbd",
                                                "text": "[…] a withered tree, through husbands toyle,\n Is often seene full freshly to have florisht […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "355f8445-947c-4c81-8f00-c18dc0b7f17d",
                                                "sense_id": "78fbca52-16fd-3760-b48e-bca1966a9bbd",
                                                "text": "The painfull husband plowing up his ground, Shall finde all fret and rust both pikes and shields"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1afab6c6-da20-4402-a123-b861ec83ec00",
                                                "sense_id": "78fbca52-16fd-3760-b48e-bca1966a9bbd",
                                                "text": "He is the neatest husband for curious ordering his domestick and field accommodations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbab641f-b0b4-3d49-9137-1ed95c308d1c",
                                        "entry_id": "8d0fb453-501e-3368-8251-ef83d1218bb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The male of a pair of animals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ee13232-a1b5-42a1-b789-712e74d1e29c",
                                                "sense_id": "fbab641f-b0b4-3d49-9137-1ed95c308d1c",
                                                "text": "Husband of the Herd"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbfb191f-89bb-35d4-9aec-4560036afd84",
                                        "entry_id": "8d0fb453-501e-3368-8251-ef83d1218bb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large cushion with arms meant to support a person in the sitting position; a husband pillow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5a5f372-d2ff-4c5a-92e4-c4ce33162e97",
                                                "sense_id": "fbfb191f-89bb-35d4-9aec-4560036afd84",
                                                "text": "While reading her book, Sally leaned back against her husband, wishing it were the human kind."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3b3082d-d786-35fc-b3c4-b73210755549",
                                        "entry_id": "8d0fb453-501e-3368-8251-ef83d1218bb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A polled tree; a pollard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "husband",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ba4254e-07ff-36e8-a496-615599b87ef9",
                                        "entry_id": "024c7cbc-99bd-38eb-8198-0a785d8412c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To manage or administer carefully and frugally; use to the best advantage; economise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ad90ad5-1579-4928-a78f-4c763dfb5a0c",
                                                "sense_id": "2ba4254e-07ff-36e8-a496-615599b87ef9",
                                                "text": "And for my meanes, I'll husband them so well,\nThey shall go farre with little."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f94dff1a-efef-35f2-908d-cbe01ba01bf2",
                                        "entry_id": "024c7cbc-99bd-38eb-8198-0a785d8412c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To conserve."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92040f1b-55b3-4523-8293-bf924207115b",
                                                "sense_id": "f94dff1a-efef-35f2-908d-cbe01ba01bf2",
                                                "text": "1719, Daniel Defoe, Robinson Crusoe\n...I found pens, ink, and paper, and I husbanded them to the utmost; and I shall show that while my ink lasted, I kept things very exact, but after that was gone I could not, for I could not make any ink by any means that I could devise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e695cc72-cd9c-3926-9fd1-ba8e4a8f16c7",
                                        "entry_id": "024c7cbc-99bd-38eb-8198-0a785d8412c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To till; cultivate; farm; nurture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fedb1cd3-aca3-4c21-a498-5ee038e42d2a",
                                                "sense_id": "e695cc72-cd9c-3926-9fd1-ba8e4a8f16c7",
                                                "text": "Land so trim and rarely husbanded."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f28781e-a1b8-3dbd-844c-52c974adb955",
                                        "entry_id": "024c7cbc-99bd-38eb-8198-0a785d8412c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To provide with a husband."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cdabf1e-8c96-45b8-ac76-b27e8bb789e8",
                                                "sense_id": "4f28781e-a1b8-3dbd-844c-52c974adb955",
                                                "text": "Thinke you, I am no ſtronger then my Sex\n Being ſo Father'd, and ſo Husbanded?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c71eedd7-ee62-34df-b6bb-36024a3f0b49",
                                        "entry_id": "024c7cbc-99bd-38eb-8198-0a785d8412c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To engage or act as a husband to; assume the care of or responsibility for; accept as one's own."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
